Package: sconjoint
Title: Structural Deep-Learning Estimation for Conjoint Experiments
Version: 0.3.0.9000
Date: 2026-08-23
Authors@R: c(
    person("Avidit", "Acharya", role = "aut"),
    person("Jens", "Hainmueller", role = "aut"),
    person("Yiqing", "Xu", , "yiqingxu@stanford.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Implements a respondent-sequence low-rank normal mixed-logit
    model for forced-choice conjoint experiments. A deep neural-network
    sieve represents the covariate-dependent conditional mean of latent
    preferences, while a jointly estimated low-rank covariance represents
    persistent residual heterogeneity. The package separates full-sample
    structural plug-in estimation, respondent-level cross-fitted one-step
    inference for prespecified regular rowwise-expectation primitives and
    named smooth transformations under explicit high-level conditions, and
    design/specification assessment. It does not claim
    recovery of realized respondent preferences with bounded task counts or
    automatic verification of normality, rank, neural-network rates, or
    numerical-integration error rates. Builds on 'torch' for the
    deep-learning backend.
